# Test Data Attributes Standard

All interactive elements and testable components MUST include `data-testid` attributes for stable E2E test selectors.

## Philosophy

**Stable selectors prevent test brittleness.** CSS classes, DOM structure, and text content change frequently. `data-testid` attributes are semantic, stable, and intended solely for testing.

## Naming Convention

```
data-testid="{module}-{component}-{element}-{action}"
```

**Rules:**
- Use kebab-case (lowercase with dashes)
- Be descriptive but concise
- Include module prefix for context
- Include action for interactive elements

## Required Elements by Module

### Global Navigation

```html
<!-- Main navigation -->
<nav>
  <a routerLink="/" data-testid="nav-home">Home</a>
  <a routerLink="/explore" data-testid="nav-explore">Explore</a>
  <a routerLink="/build" data-testid="nav-build">Build</a>
  <a routerLink="/report" data-testid="nav-report">Report</a>
</nav>

<!-- Target location dropdown (always visible) -->
<div data-testid="target-location-dropdown">
  <span data-testid="target-location-display">Denver, CO</span>
  <button data-testid="target-location-clear">×</button>
</div>
```

### Explore Module

