## Naming Patterns

### Common Patterns

| Element Type | Pattern | Example |
|--------------|---------|---------|
| Button | `{module}-{action}-button` | `build-save-button` |
| Input | `{module}-{field}-input` | `build-land-cost-input` |
| Link | `{module}-{target}-link` | `explore-comparables-link` |
| Container | `{module}-{section}-container` | `explore-map-container` |
| List | `{module}-{items}-list` | `build-proforma-list` |
| List Item | `{module}-{item}-item-{id}` | `build-proforma-item-1` |
| Display | `{module}-{data}-display` | `build-calculated-noi` |
| Message | `{module}-{type}-message` | `build-error-message` |

### Dynamic IDs

For lists or repeated elements, append an index or unique ID:

```html
<!-- Static ID (single element) -->
<button data-testid="create-proforma-button">Create</button>

<!-- Dynamic ID (list items) -->
<div data-testid="proforma-item-1">Proforma 1</div>
<div data-testid="proforma-item-2">Proforma 2</div>

<!-- Or use semantic ID -->
<div data-testid="proforma-item-denver">Denver Property</div>
```

## Implementation Guidelines

### Angular Components

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Add data-testid to template
@Component({
  selector: 'app-build',
  template: `
    <div data-testid="build-page">
      <button
        data-testid="build-create-proforma-button"
        (click)="createProforma()">
        Create Proforma
      </button>
    </div>
  `
})
export class BuildComponent {
  createProforma() { }
}
```

### Dynamic Attributes

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Dynamic data-testid with ngFor
@Component({
  template: `
    @for (proforma of proformas; track proforma.id) {
      <div [attr.data-testid]="'proforma-item-' + proforma.id">
        {{ proforma.name }}
      </div>
    }
  `
})
```

### Conditional Elements

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: data-testid on conditional elements
@Component({
  template: `
    @if (error) {
      <div data-testid="build-error-message">
        {{ error }}
      </div>
    }

    @if (success) {
      <div data-testid="build-save-success">
        Saved successfully!
      </div>
    }
  `
})
```

## What NOT to Use as Selectors

### ❌ BAD: CSS Classes

```html
<!-- ❌ DON'T: CSS classes change with styling -->
<button class="btn-primary">Submit</button>
```

**Why:** Classes are for styling. They change frequently with design updates.

### ❌ BAD: Element Position

```typescript
// ❌ DON'T: Nth-child selectors
await page.click('button:nth-child(3)');
```

**Why:** DOM structure changes. Adding/removing elements breaks tests.

### ❌ BAD: Text Content

```typescript
// ❌ DON'T: Text selectors
await page.click('text=Submit');
```

**Why:** Copy changes. Internationalization breaks tests.

### ❌ BAD: Element IDs (usually)

```html
<!-- ❌ DON'T: IDs for styling -->
<button id="submit-btn">Submit</button>
```

**Why:** IDs are often used for JavaScript/styling, not testing. They may conflict or change.

## Using data-testid in Tests

### Page Object Model

```typescript
// page-objects/build/build-page.ts
export class BuildPage {
  readonly createButton = this.page.locator('[data-testid="build-create-proforma-button"]');
  readonly nameInput = this.page.locator('[data-testid="build-proforma-name-input"]');
  readonly saveButton = this.page.locator('[data-testid="build-save-button"]');

  constructor(private page: Page) {}

  async createProforma(name: string) {
    await this.createButton.click();
    await this.nameInput.fill(name);
    await this.saveButton.click();
  }
}
```

### Direct Usage in Tests

```typescript
test('user can create proforma', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.click('[data-testid="build-create-proforma-button"]');
  await page.fill('[data-testid="build-proforma-name-input"]', 'Test');
  await page.click('[data-testid="build-save-button"]');

  await expect(page.locator('[data-testid="build-save-success"]'))
    .toBeVisible();
});
```

## Verification

### How to Verify Attributes Are Added

Use Playwright MCP to inspect page:

```
1. browser_navigate to http://localhost:4200/build
2. browser_snapshot
3. Verify output shows data-testid attributes
```

Or check browser DevTools:
```javascript
// In browser console
document.querySelectorAll('[data-testid]').length
```

## Migration Strategy

### For Existing Code

1. **Identify interactive elements** without data-testid
2. **Add attributes** following naming convention
3. **Update tests** to use new selectors
4. **Verify tests pass** with new selectors
5. **Remove old selectors** from tests

### Priority Order

1. **Critical journey elements** (P0)
   - Navigation buttons
   - Create/save/delete buttons
   - Primary input fields

2. **Module-specific elements** (P1)
   - Secondary actions
   - Display elements
   - Lists

3. **Edge case elements** (P2)
   - Error messages
   - Success messages
   - Optional features

## Exceptions

### When NOT to Add data-testid

- **Purely decorative elements** (icons, dividers)
- **Non-interactive text** (unless displayed value needs verification)
- **Internal implementation details** (not tested)
- **Third-party components** (use library-provided selectors)

## Checklist for New Components

When creating a new Angular component:

- [ ] Add `data-testid` to page container
- [ ] Add `data-testid` to all buttons
- [ ] Add `data-testid` to all inputs/forms
- [ ] Add `data-testid` to all links
- [ ] Add `data-testid` to all display elements (if tested)
- [ ] Add `data-testid` to success/error messages
- [ ] Follow naming convention
- [ ] Verify in browser DevTools
- [ ] Update page object model
- [ ] Write E2E test using data-testid

